{"title":"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is equilateral with side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />, and circumradius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> (radius of the circumscribed circle). \nTriangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is equilateral with side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, and circumradius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is different from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, then: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b4f5b125032628d0b0c56ce45bebf4fb58c7847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ P:p = R:r \\text{ } \\text{only sometimes} \\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(B)}\\ P:p = R:r \\text{ } \\text{always}\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ P:p = K:k \\text{ } \\text{only sometimes} \\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ R:r = K:k \\text{ } \\text{always}\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ R:r = K:k \\text{ } \\text{only sometimes}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"255\" height=\"96\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643a4eaabe25743af769e2ec2fa1997940394802.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A=(0,50),O=(0,0),B=(43.301,-25),C=(-43.301,-25); draw(A--B--C--A); draw(circle(O,50)); draw(B--O--C); draw(anglemark(C,O,B,200)); draw((0,0)--(0,-25)); label(&quot;$60^{\\circ}$&quot;,(-7,-12)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>First, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.  Since all sides of an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equilateral_triangle\" title=\"Equilateral triangle\">equilateral triangle</a> are the same, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/1/dd1d6fedf7b7211ef5d6df41be0c905b46c11a95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=3A$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />.  From the area formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2dac4fbcd3cd628ba9ce862e4cd1362901157b60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K=\\frac{A^2\\sqrt{3}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"41\" />.  By using 30-60-90 triangles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af1c4015823fc949b5c5ad7feadb599af1f63ea7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R=\\frac{A\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Using the same steps, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/9271dcaa0540fce2ecefb76b17bc216fb5c7de21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=3a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084a2d7bd529b4c47f5f7f059a1a92e1e2429a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=\\frac{a^2\\sqrt{3}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"41\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a13fe338582adc10fced24f09273375c2536de1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{a\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/a/82ae9e86d37b47b2a83bae133cf72556cce7013b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P/p = 3A/3a = A/a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/69030521006e900e4be9ba64da867c7074790956.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R/r = \\frac{A\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\div \\frac{a\\sqrt{3}}{3} = A/a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"214\" height=\"41\" />.  That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d5679a192856ca75bae86a0fc5995e7fbb3b9c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P/p = R/r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME\" title=\"1960 AHSME\">1960 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1960 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1960\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/P